A||||1||85fierose||throttle body/injector gasket||||10||
Z||000000||85fierose||03-31-2000||01:00 AM||||In case anyone has recently removed the cover  on the throttle which holds the injector in place you will notice that there is a seal around the caseing. I tore mine when i removed the injector. Fortunatly, i was able to get a piece of gasket material from the local auto parts store and trace and cut a new gasket from the pieces of the old. It has given me no problems since....just a tip from someone that has been there.||||reg||10
Z||000001||theogre||03-31-2000||10:46 PM||||It can be done that way if you're in a pinch or are sure every thing else is ok. <P>Otherwise get the rebuild kit. It's not real expensive and it gives you a chance to clean out all the rest of the TBI unit. Likely if you have an ijector issue you'll want to do that to protect the new injector from fouling with dirt.||||reg||1
